      "content": "hey, i was looking at some atmospheric readings from november 17th and realized i've been hearing this weird low-frequency hum/static in my apartment for a while now. is it physically possible for low-frequency data streams to be transmitted through the air via atmospheric refraction or something? like, could the air itself be carrying encoded signals?",
